{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Bitumen pits, pits of clay.</b> There were many pits there, from which earth is taken for building mortar. And its midrash — that the clay hardened around them, and a miracle was done for the king of Sodom that he emerged from there, because some of the nations did not believe that Abraham was saved from Ur Kasdim from the burning of the fire, and once this one emerged from the clay, they believed in Abraham retroactively." "<b>To the mountain they fled.</b> To the mountain they fled — הֶרָה is like לְהָר. Any word that needs a lamed at its beginning, Scripture placed a heh at its end. And there is a distinction between הֶרָה and הָהָרָה: the heh at the end of the word stands in place of the lamed at its beginning, but it does not stand in place of a lamed with a patach under it — so הֶרָה is like לְהַר or like אֶל הַר, and it does not specify to which mountain, but each one fled to whatever mountain he found first. But when he gives a heh at the beginning, to write הָהָרָה or הַמִּדְבָּרָה, its meaning is like אֶל הָהָר or like לְהָהָר, and it means that specific, explicitly identified mountain in the passage."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:39.204358278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}